    "result_text": "All tests pass. The change is complete and the build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented optional owner email support end-to-end, following the project's standard Spring/OpenAPI conventions.\n\n**What \"email\" now does:**\n- Optional on the owner payload. When present it must be a syntactically valid address (else `400`); it is stored and returned lower-cased. When omitted, creation succeeds normally.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added an optional `email` property (`type: string`, `format: email`, `maxLength: 255`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. The OpenAPI generator turns `format: email` into a `@Email` bean-validation constraint on the generated `OwnerFieldsDto`, and since the request body is `@Valid`, an invalid address triggers `MethodArgumentNotValidException`, which the existing `ExceptionControllerAdvice` maps to `400`. A null/omitted value passes `@Email`. `email` also flows automatically into the flattened `OwnerDto` (returned by GET).\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added the `email` field with `@Column(name = \"email\")`, a `@Email` constraint, and getter/setter. MapStruct maps it by name, no mapper change needed.\n\n3. **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres` `schema.sql`) \u2014 Added a nullable `email` column to the `owners` table.\n\n4. **`db/hsqldb/data.sql`** \u2014 The seed inserts used positional `VALUES` (no column list), which broke once a column was added, so I gave them an explicit column list. (h2/postgres already used explicit lists.)\n\n5. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 Added a `normalizeEmail` helper that lower-cases a supplied email (leaving blank/null untouched), applied in both `addOwner` and `updateOwner`.\n\n**Tests:** The full suite (`AcceptanceTest`: lowercasing, invalid\u2192400, missing\u21922xx) passes \u2014 `Tests run: 3, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, BUILD SUCCESS.",
